@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`

-- The "highest layer" sentence: "the gain shall be regarded as the highest layer in the scale of the taxable income", with a rate "not
-- exceeding" a cap. It appears in the Income Tax Ordinance at s 91(b)(1) (source line 3347), s 91(b1)(2) (line 3360) and s 125C(b) (line 4530);
-- this module is the one place that turns the sentence into arithmetic, so that the three sections share it.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt (sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6).
--
-- WHAT IT DOES. The seller's other taxable income fills the scale of s 121 from the bottom; the gain is a further layer of that income,
-- above it. The tax on the gain is what the bands it falls in charge, each at its own rate, the rate being "not more than" the cap.
-- Two things are not decided by the text and are forks (NOTES.md): T1, how the cap applies where the gain stands in several bands (each
-- shekel at the lesser of its band's rate and the cap, or the whole at the lesser of the average rate and the cap); T2 (in
-- ito-91-capital-gains.l4), where each part of a gain taxed in three parts stands within the layer.
--
-- THE SCALE IS AN INPUT. The caller lists the bands of s 121 that apply to the individual (the scale of (a), or the scale of (b)(1) for
-- income from personal exertion or an individual of 60; which applies to a gain is s 121's business, row IL-03), lowest band first, the last
-- band with no upper limit. Credit points and the additional tax of s 121B are not part of the layer's tax here.

§ `The highest layer of the taxable income`

-- src:3347 | (ב)(1) יחיד יהיה חייב במס על רווח הון ריאלי כאמור בסעיף 121, בשיעור שלא יעלה על 25%, ויראו את רווח ההון כשלב הגבוה ביותר בסולם הכנסתו החייבת.
-- src:3360 | (2) לענין סעיף קטן זה, יראו את רווח ההון כשלב הגבוה ביותר בסולם ההכנסה החייבת.
-- src:4530 | (ב) יחיד חייב במס על הכנסה מריבית בשיעור שלא יעלה על 25%, ויראו את הכנסתו זו כשלב הגבוה ביותר בסולם הכנסתו החייבת.

§§ `The overlap of a layer with a band, and the tax of a layer through a list of bands`

-- How much of the layer from a to b lies in the band from `lower` to `upper` (NOTHING: no upper limit).
GIVEN a     IS A NUMBER
      b     IS A NUMBER
      lower IS A NUMBER
      upper IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part of the layer from` a `to` b `lying in the band from` lower `up to` upper MEANS
    CONSIDER upper
    WHEN JUST u  THEN max 0 (min b u MINUS max a lower)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN max 0 (b MINUS max a lower)

-- Where the next band starts: at the top of this one, or nowhere (the last band).
GIVEN lower IS A NUMBER
      upper IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the start of the band after one from` lower `up to` upper MEANS
    CONSIDER upper
    WHEN JUST u  THEN u
    WHEN NOTHING THEN lower

-- The tax of the layer from a to b through the bands, each band's rate taken at most at the cap.
GIVEN bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      lower IS A NUMBER
      a     IS A NUMBER
      b     IS A NUMBER
      cap   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax of the layer through` bands `from the lower limit` lower `for the layer from` a `to` b `with each rate at most` cap MEANS
    CONSIDER bands
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN band FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        min (band's `rate of the band`) cap TIMES `the part of the layer from` a `to` b `lying in the band from` lower `up to` (band's `upper limit of the band`)
        PLUS `the tax of the layer through` rest `from the lower limit` (`the start of the band after one from` lower `up to` (band's `upper limit of the band`)) `for the layer from` a `to` b `with each rate at most` cap

§§ `The tax of one layer, at one reading of the cap`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent` MEANS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the way of applying the cap is not decided and here it changes the answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "the way a cap on the rate applies where the gain stands in several bands is not decided by the text, and here it changes the answer"

-- At an explicit reading of fork T1.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(1), (b1)(2); s 125C(b) (source lines 3347, 3360, 4530); fork T1
GIVEN g     IS A NUMBER
      a     IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      cap   IS A NUMBER
      r     IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on a layer of` g `standing on the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `with the rate capped at` cap `, applying the cap as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the rate of each band is capped`                                         THEN `each`
    WHEN `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`                          THEN `average`
    WHEN `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`
      THEN IF   `each` EQUALS `average`
           THEN `each`
           ELSE `the way of applying the cap is not decided and here it changes the answer`
    WHERE
        `each` MEANS `the tax of the layer through` bands `from the lower limit` 0 `for the layer from` a `to` (a PLUS g) `with each rate at most` cap
        `uncapped` MEANS `the tax of the layer through` bands `from the lower limit` 0 `for the layer from` a `to` (a PLUS g) `with each rate at most` `these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent`
        `average` MEANS min `uncapped` (cap TIMES g)

-- The explicit readings of fork T1, the one named or both where it is declined.
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
`the explicit readings of the cap in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the rate of each band is capped`                                         THEN LIST `the rate of each band is capped`
    WHEN `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`                          THEN LIST `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`
    WHEN `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`
      THEN LIST `the rate of each band is capped`, `the average rate over the whole gain is capped`

-- The explicit readings of fork T2.
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
`the explicit readings of where the parts stand in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `each part stands alone on top of the other income`                       THEN LIST `each part stands alone on top of the other income`
    WHEN `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest`           THEN LIST `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest`
    WHEN `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest`          THEN LIST `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest`
    WHEN `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
      THEN LIST `each part stands alone on top of the other income`, `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest`, `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest`

-- The common value of a list of numbers: JUST it if they are all the same and there is at least one, NOTHING otherwise.
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the common value of` xs MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY                  THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest     THEN IF all (GIVEN y YIELD y EQUALS x) rest THEN JUST x ELSE NOTHING

-- The tax of one layer at the reading of fork T1 the caller names, the answer where the readings agree and a refusal where they part.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(1), (b1)(2); s 125C(b) (source lines 3347, 3360, 4530); fork T1; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN g     IS A NUMBER
      a     IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      cap   IS A NUMBER
      r     IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on the top layer` g `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `with the rate capped at` cap `, reading the cap as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answers at every reading left open`
    WHEN JUST v  THEN v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the way of applying the cap is not decided and here it changes the answer`
    WHERE
        `the answers at every reading left open` MEANS
            `the common value of` (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the tax on a layer of` g `standing on the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `with the rate capped at` cap `, applying the cap as` t) (`the explicit readings of the cap in` r))

§§ `Three parts of one gain in the top layer (section 91(b1), (e)(2))`

-- One part: its size, where it starts above the other income, its own cap.
GIVEN g     IS A NUMBER
      off   IS A NUMBER
      c     IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      cap   IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax of the part` g `standing at` off `with the rate capped at` c `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap MEANS
    `the tax on a layer of` g `standing on the other taxable income` off `under the scale` bands `with the rate capped at` c `, applying the cap as` cap

-- The three parts of a gain, each with its own cap, stand in the top layer in the order fork T2 names. Part 1 is the earliest period.
-- The offsets: alone, each above the other income; earliest lowest, part 1 above the other income, part 2 above that, part 3 above that;
-- earliest highest, the reverse.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1)-(2) (source lines 3352-3360); forks T1, T2
GIVEN g1 IS A NUMBER
      g2 IS A NUMBER
      g3 IS A NUMBER
      c1 IS A NUMBER
      c2 IS A NUMBER
      c3 IS A NUMBER
      a  IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      cap   IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o     IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax of three parts` g1 `and` g2 `and` g3 `capped at` c1 `and` c2 `and` c3 `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap `, with the parts placed as` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `each part stands alone on top of the other income` THEN
          `the tax of the part` g1 `standing at` a `with the rate capped at` c1 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g2 `standing at` a `with the rate capped at` c2 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g3 `standing at` a `with the rate capped at` c3 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
    WHEN `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period lowest` THEN
          `the tax of the part` g1 `standing at` a `with the rate capped at` c1 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g2 `standing at` (a PLUS g1) `with the rate capped at` c2 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g3 `standing at` (a PLUS g1 PLUS g2) `with the rate capped at` c3 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
    WHEN `the parts stand one above another, the earliest period highest` THEN
          `the tax of the part` g3 `standing at` a `with the rate capped at` c3 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g2 `standing at` (a PLUS g3) `with the rate capped at` c2 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
        PLUS `the tax of the part` g1 `standing at` (a PLUS g3 PLUS g2) `with the rate capped at` c1 `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` cap
    WHEN `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer` THEN 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the place of each part in the top layer is not decided and here it changes the answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "the place of each part of a gain within the top layer is not decided by the text, and here it changes the answer"

-- The three parts at the readings the caller names: the answer where every reading left open gives the same one, a refusal where they part.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1)-(2) (source lines 3352-3360); forks T1, T2; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN g1 IS A NUMBER
      g2 IS A NUMBER
      g3 IS A NUMBER
      c1 IS A NUMBER
      c2 IS A NUMBER
      c3 IS A NUMBER
      a  IS A NUMBER
      bands IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      cap   IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o     IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax of three parts, at the readings,` g1 `and` g2 `and` g3 `capped at` c1 `and` c2 `and` c3 `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the cap as` cap `and the places of the parts as` o MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answers at every reading left open`
    WHEN JUST v  THEN v
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF   `the caps split` THEN `the way of applying the cap is not decided and here it changes the answer`
        ELSE `the place of each part in the top layer is not decided and here it changes the answer`
    WHERE
        `the answers at every reading left open` MEANS
            `the common value of` (concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD
                                                  map (GIVEN p YIELD `the tax of three parts` g1 `and` g2 `and` g3 `capped at` c1 `and` c2 `and` c3 `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` t `, with the parts placed as` p)
                                                      (`the explicit readings of where the parts stand in` o))
                                              (`the explicit readings of the cap in` cap)))
        -- Which fork is to blame: the places are fixed and the answers still part, so it is the cap; else the places.
        `the caps split` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the common value of` (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the tax of three parts` g1 `and` g2 `and` g3 `capped at` c1 `and` c2 `and` c3 `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` t `, with the parts placed as` `each part stands alone on top of the other income`) (`the explicit readings of the cap in` cap))
            WHEN JUST w  THEN FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
